The remote `public.payments` table has no `client_reference` column, so I used the existing staff-only `RETURNING *` insert path instead of trying to set a field that doesn’t exist. That means the `local-remote-pay-001` value is just a local tracking reference I used for SQL, not a column stored on the remote row. If you want the frontend/app UI to be able to create payments with an ID or client reference while it is running, that would need a small app/schema change and a separate review of the insert policy.

