## ✅ Fixed — 404 on direct links resolved

**Cause:** Netlify had no SPA redirect rule, so any direct visit to a client-side route (`/auth/login`, `/auth/forgot-password`, …) returned Netlify's 404 page instead of serving the Angular app.

**Fix:** Added a catch-all redirect to [netlify.toml](netlify.toml):

```toml
[build]
  command = "npm run build"
  publish = "dist/turf-academy-ui/browser"

[[redirects]]
  from = "/*"
  to = "/index.html"
  status = 200
```

**What I did:**
1. Identified `netlify.toml` had the correct publish directory but no redirect rule
2. Added the `/* → /index.html` SPA redirect (status 200, so Angular's router keeps control of the URL)
3. Committed as `af30843` — *"fix: add SPA redirect rule to netlify.toml for client-side routing"*
4. Pushed to GitHub, waited for Netlify to redeploy

